Cabildo dataset isolation profiles

The seccomp profile and AppArmor base are derived from moby/profiles
revision 2ceae35d351c156cb5a8efc0fdc4a08cf94569d8:
https://github.com/moby/profiles/tree/2ceae35d351c156cb5a8efc0fdc4a08cf94569d8
Copyright The Moby Authors. Licensed under Apache-2.0 (see LICENSE.moby).

Cabildo additions allow Bubblewrap namespace creation with CLONE_NEWUSER
and CLONE_NEWNS, nested user namespaces, and private root setup. AppArmor
limits the added mount operations to Bubblewrap's scratch root and its
three read-only files (jq, input.json, filter.jq).

The Docker capability set and host sysctls are not expanded. These profiles
are configured for the development Compose backend. Install the named
AppArmor profile on the node with install-dataset-isolation.sh before use.
